{"name":"Mystic River","hex":"#b7cae0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mystic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, or relating to mystics, mysticism or occult mysteries; mystical.","Mysterious and strange; arcane, obscure or enigmatic."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who practices mysticism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mystic"},{"term":"river","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large and often winding stream which drains a land mass, carrying water down from higher areas to a lower point, oftentimes ending in another body of water, such as an ocean or in an inland sea.","Any large flow of a liquid in a single body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To improve one’s hand to beat another player on the final card in a poker game."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/river"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mystic River","blocks":[{"text":"The Mystic River is a 7.0-mile-long (11.3 km) river in Massachusetts. In the Massachusett language, missi-tuk means \"large estuary\", alluding to the tidal nature of the Mystic River. The resemblance to the English word mystic is a coincidence, which the colonists followed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystic_River","wikidata":"Q1758000"},{"title":"Mystic River (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mystic River is a 2003 American neo-noir mystery crime drama film. It was directed and co-produced by Clint Eastwood, and stars Sean Penn, Tim Robbins, Kevin Bacon, Laurence Fishburne, Marcia Gay Harden, and Laura Linney. The screenplay, written by Brian Helgeland, was based on the 2001 novel by Dennis Lehane. It is the first film in which Eastwood was credited as composer of the score."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/Mystic_River_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mystic_River_(film)","wikidata":"Q221586"},{"title":"River","blocks":[{"text":"A river is a natural stream of fresh water that flows on land or inside caves towards another body of water at a lower elevation, such as an ocean, lake, or another river. A river may run dry before reaching the end of its course if it runs out of water, or only flow during certain seasons. Rivers are regulated by the water cycle, the processes by which water moves around the Earth. Water first enters rivers through precipitation, whether from rainfall, the runoff of water down a slope, the melting of glaciers or snow, or seepage from aquifers beneath the surface of the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg/330px-Pirogue_running_on_the_Mekong_at_golden_hour_between_Don_Det_and_Don_Khon_Laos.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/River","wikidata":"Q4022"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Mystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMystic_River_in_Medford_MA_2014.tif"},{"srcset